<title>INDIA: INDIA SAYS TO REPAY GOVT STOCK ON SEPTEMBER 1.</title>
<headline>INDIA SAYS TO REPAY GOVT STOCK ON SEPTEMBER 1.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Indian government said the outstanding balance of its 1997, 13.5 percent loan will become repayable at par on September 1.</p>
<p>&quot;No interest will accrue on the loan as from the said date,&quot; the Finance Ministry said in a statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The repayment of the loan will see over 50 billion rupees released into the banking system, dealers said.</p>
<p>--Bombay Newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
